Daniel Nilsson wrote:

> I think my biggest mistake was to continue down so far without being
> prepared for all the nasties there. Should probably have gone up to the
> mines and clear out them instead. Where is a good place to turn in the main
> dungeon?

As soon as you finish Sokoban.

Conventional wisdom seems to be to do Minetown and Sokoban
(in either order) and then mine's end. Luck (in game) is
very important in this game and even if you are able to
increase your luck, unless you have a luckstone, it'll just
drain away. Once you get the luckstone, there are a couple
of straight forward ways to increase your luck.

I think that Minetown is more valuable than Sokoban, so when
I find the stairs, I check it out immediately. If it's dark
on the first mine level, I won't stray far from the stairs,
but I will try to score a pick ax and/or some armor with a
quick foray. I once had a character go from AC 6 to -9
without going 5 steps from the base of the stairs, he
ascended IIRC!

If the first mine level isn't lit, I'll turn back after my
raid and head for Sokoban. If the level is lit, I'll try to
finish it and check out the next mine level. If I can reach
Minetown, I feel like I'm off to a good start.

